                                "sense_id": "422b4e49-1909-30c6-b25e-74a2befe5636",
                                "text": "He concisely explains that Whig histories tend to \"praise revolutions [for history of science, we could read novelties, ideas or individuals] provided they have been successful, emphasise certain principles of progress in the past and produce a story which is the ratification if not the glorification of the present\"."
